#
# No splash screen while Plasma starts (desktop-experience.md, 6.4): the sign
# that the desktop is ready is the desktop. Plasma 6.8 starts its splash
# unless Engine is something other than KSplashQML (startkde/startplasma.cpp).
#
# The group is locked ([$i], KDE's "immutable" mark). Without the lock this
# file would not be enough: whenever a global theme is applied, at every
# sign-in included, Plasma writes Engine=KSplashQML into the account's
# defaults, which come before this file. Every global theme has a splash as
# far as Plasma is concerned, because a theme without one falls back to
# Breeze's (libklookandfeel/klookandfeelmanager.cpp; seen in the boot test).
# The price: the splash cannot be chosen in System Settings.

[KSplash][$i]
Engine=none
Theme=None
